/span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb P\">\\(\\mathbb P\\)</span> (forcing poset)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_{\\mathbb P}\">\\(\\leq_{\\mathbb P}\\)</span> (forcing order)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"1_{\\mathbb P}\">\\(1_{\\mathbb P}\\)</span> (top condition)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\in\\mathbb P\">\\(p\\in\\mathbb P\\)</span> (condition)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> (transitive ground model for the forcing relation)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (language signature)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span> (formula)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2ForcingPoset}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2ForcingPoset}_S\\)</span> (forcing-poset predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"b5833df5ef175153\" href=\"?note=b5833df5ef175153\" title=\"58-df-zfc-forcing2-forcing-poset\">58-df-zfc-forcing2-forcing-poset</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TransitiveSet}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{TransitiveSet}_S\\)</span> (ground-model guard, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"c14ba496c480dcd6\" href=\"?note=c14ba496c480dcd6\" title=\"58-df-transitive-set\">58-df-transitive-set</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Vdash_{M,\\mathbb P}\">\\(\\Vdash_{M,\\mathbb P}\\)</span> (forcing relation, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"46b2495f214783c3\" href=\"?note=46b2495f214783c3\" title=\"58-df-forcing-relation\">58-df-forcing-relation</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2DecidesFormula}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2DecidesFormula}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing2\\text{-}decides\\text{-}formula} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcForcing2DecidesFormula}_S(p,\\varphi,M,\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P},\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{TransitiveSet}_S(M)\\land\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P}\\in M\\land\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2ForcingPoset}_S(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P})\\land p\\in\\mathbb P\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\bigl(p\\Vdash_{M,\\mathbb P}\\varphi\\lor p\\Vdash_{M,\\mathbb P}\\neg\\varphi\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing2\\text{-}decides\\text{-}formula} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcForcing2DecidesFormula}_S(p,\\varphi,M,\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P},\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{TransitiveSet}_S(M)\\land\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P}\\in M\\land\\mathrm{ZfcForcing2ForcingPoset}_S(\\mathbb P,\\leq_{\\mathbb P},1_{\\mathbb P})\\land p\\in\\mathbb P\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\bigl(p\\Vdash_{M,\\mathbb P}\\varphi\\lor p\\Vdash_{M,\\mathbb P}\\neg\\varphi\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Auxiliary ZFC definition.</li>\n<li><code>58-df-zfc-forcing4-decides-formula</code> is merged here; it used the same forcing-or-negation decision condition.</li>\n<li>Alias predicates are downstream wrappers around this base predicate.</li>\n<li>The ground model is explicit and now guarded as a transitive set containing the forcing data, as required by the model-relative forcing relation.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3